  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening national efforts to prevent trafficking in persons and rehabilitate victims of trafficking in the Republic of Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen national capacities to identify and provide tailored rehabilitation assistance to (potential) Victims of Trafficking (VoTs) in the Republic of Moldova, adapted to the refugee context caused by the Russian invasion of Ukraine. IOM will contribute to awareness raising of safe travel and available services among at-risk groups, particularly those on the move, ensuring visibility to information and identification services provided through the national Anti-Trafficking Hot-Lines run by &quot;La Strada&quot; and the NGO &quot;Interaction&apos;, and supporting State authorities in the provision of tailored assistance. In addition, the project will support the relevant governmental structures to identify and assist Unaccompanied and/or Separated Children (UASCs) through the application of the legal procedures in relation to the protection of UASCs, and in the best interests of the child, including their referral, onward movement, alternative care, family tracing and reunification, and ensuring their protection is in line with the national legislation and international standards.</narrative>
  </description>
